# --- Environment: NEVER commit real secrets -------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.test is committed DELIBERATELY. It contains ONLY dummy values pointing at
# the disposable test container on port 5433 — no secret, no real host, no real
# credential. Committing it is what makes `npm test` work from a fresh clone.
# Any variable already in the process environment overrides it, so CI can still
# point the suite elsewhere. REVIEW ANY CHANGE TO IT: a real value here is a
# leaked value.
!.env.test
# .env.ci.example is committed for the same reason, and was previously excluded
# by ACCIDENT: `.env.*` matched it and no negation followed, so README.md and
# RUNBOOK.md both referenced a file that was never in the repository and a fresh
# clone could not run `npm run build`. It holds only `.invalid` dummy values.
# 🔴 `.env.ci` itself — the filled-in copy — stays ignored.
!.env.ci.example

# --- Node / Next -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# --- Local upload storage (dev fallback when CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME is unset) -
/media/
/documents/

